@anon.9bf146a73cb71d9c7e3fe69f46c42f4a.568 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [217 x i8] }> <{ [217 x i8] c"How to [number]($numbering) block-level equations.\0A\0A```example\0A#set math.equation(numbering: \22(1)\22)\0A\0AWe define:\0A$ phi.alt := (1 + sqrt(5)) / 2 $ <ratio>\0A\0AWith @ratio, we get:\0A$ F_n = floor(1 / sqrt(5) phi.alt^n) $\0A```" }>, align 1
@anon.9bf146a73cb71d9c7e3fe69f46c42f4a.569 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [422 x i8] }> <{ [422 x i8] c"The alignment of the equation numbering.\0A\0ABy default, the alignment is `{end + horizon}`. For the horizontal\0Acomponent, you can use `{right}`, `{left}`, or `{start}` and `{end}`\0Aof the text direction; for the vertical component, you can use\0A`{top}`, `{horizon}`, or `{bottom}`.\0A\0A```example\0A#set math.equation(numbering: \22(1)\22, number-align: bottom)\0A\0AWe can calculate:\0A$ E &= sqrt(m_0^2 + p^2) \\\0A    &approx 125 \22GeV\22 $\0A```" }>, align 1
@anon.9bf146a73cb71d9c7e3fe69f46c42f4a.570 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [383 x i8] }> <{ [383 x i8] c"A supplement for the equation.\0A\0AFor references to equations, this is added before the referenced number.\0A\0AIf a function is specified, it is passed the referenced equation and\0Ashould return content.\0A\0A```example\0A#set math.equation(numbering: \22(1)\22, supplement: [Eq.])\0A\0AWe define:\0A$ phi.alt := (1 + sqrt(5)) / 2 $ <ratio>\0A\0AWith @ratio, we get:\0A$ F_n = floor(1 / sqrt(5) phi.alt^n) $\0A```" }>, align 1
